  "notes": "FORMS:\n{勝|しょう} (win) + {利|り} (benefit, advantage)\n\nREGISTER:\nA formal word for winning, commonly used in sports reporting, politics, military contexts, and elections. In casual speech, {勝|か}つ (to win) or {勝|か}ち (a win) is more natural.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {勝利|しょうり}を{収|おさ}める: to achieve/secure a victory\n- {勝利|しょうり}を{祝|いわ}う: to celebrate a victory\n- {圧倒的|あっとうてき}な{勝利|しょうり}: an overwhelming victory\n- {歴史的|れきしてき}{勝利|しょうり}: a historic victory\n- {逆転|ぎゃくてん}{勝利|しょうり}: come-from-behind victory\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {勝利|しょうり}: victory (formal, noun)\n- {敗北|はいぼく}: defeat (formal, the antonym)\n- {勝|か}ち: a win (casual)\n- {負|ま}け: a loss (casual)",
